{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34893-old-wod-mage-the-ascension-mummy-the-resurrection-crossover","id":34893,"title":"[Old WoD] Mage: The Ascension / Mummy: The Resurrection - crossover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-22T04:48:27-08:00","id":34893,"title":"[Old WoD] Mage: The Ascension / Mummy: The Resurrection - crossover","content":"Good day.<br /> <br /> First of all, I'm really sorry for my English. My native language is Russian and there are only a couple of months of English lessons that I took from November to nowadays.<br /> <br /> Actually, that's why I'm here. I've learn Mage from (a) unofficial russian-translations, (b) practice in real games, (c) conversations with much more knowledgeable people than me.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, there are no translations, official or not, of MtR into Russian. So I've read the corebook with my very low language skills. Well... the idea is to crossover MtA and MtR. And I have few questions about MtR setting, game world. Especially in conjunction with MtA.<br /> <br /> 1. What is the main difference between Amenti and Wu T'ian? Minor differences?<br /> 2. All of the Amenti's was created in Ancient times? Or it is possible to create new Mummy now, in the present time? If it is possible, who and how, now, not in the past, can create the new Amenti/Wu T'ian?<br /> 3. Can Awakened Mage (not linear sorcerer) become a Mummy? Is it possible for one person at the same time to be the Mage and the Mummie? If &quot;yes&quot;, are there some niceties to mention in crossover? If &quot;not&quot;, why not?<br /> <br /> Thank you very much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1775-mish","name":"Mish","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1775_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T19:38:56-08:00","id":37620,"title":"","content":"The main difference between the Wu T'ian and the Amenti is that the Amenti are a fusion of a incomplete modern soul with a fragment of an ancient soul, while the Wu T'ian are a enlightened being whose Body and Soul are fused into a single entity. <br /> <br /> The Amenti are all new creations. They are created by the various Neteru Cults. They are fusions of souls from the ancient times with modern souls. <br /> <br /> In order to become a Mummy the mage in question would have to die. Death would separate them from their Avatar. The character could go from Mage to Mummy, but would not be both at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1816-revfuggit","name":"RevFuggit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T04:35:00-08:00","id":41639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RevFuggit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34893-old-wod-mage-the-ascension-mummy-the-resurrection-crossover?p=37620#post37620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main difference between the Wu T'ian and the Amenti is that the Amenti are a fusion of a incomplete modern soul with a fragment of an ancient soul, while the Wu T'ian are a enlightened being whose Body and Soul are fused into a single entity.<br /> <br /> The Amenti are all new creations. They are created by the various Neteru Cults. They are fusions of souls from the ancient times with modern souls.<br /> <br /> In order to become a Mummy the mage in question would have to die. Death would separate them from their Avatar. The character could go from Mage to Mummy, but would not be both at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarification: in a similar -- though also opposite -- manner to becoming a Lich, a Mage doesn't lose his Avatar when becoming a mummy, but rather his Avatar is reformed/re-purposed into a different (P)aradigm (the Avatar-aspect is reflected in Mummy as the Sahu; a number of the &quot;completing spirits&quot; that create the modern Amenti are Avatars/Sahus from mummies who were mages in life -- before becoming mummies -- and said Avatars/Sahus appropriately reflect a more &quot;magical&quot;/higher view of things, as reflected in the game). The mummy-sorcerers -- both ancient and modern -- are &quot;mages&quot;, but not Mages: they trade one form of power/enlightenment for another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}